## Solution

### Fix 1 — Add capacity alerts on prod VM (≈ 30 min)
```bash
SUB=a9049f9f-3d1b-43f0-9278-7f1d603f6a00
RG=rg-normain-prod-01
VM_ID=$(az vm show -g $RG -n vmnormainprod01 --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)
AG=$(az monitor action-group show -g $RG -n ag-alerts-normain-prod-01 --query id -o tsv --subscription $SUB)

az monitor metrics alert create -n vm-cpu-alert-normain-prod-01 -g $RG --subscription $SUB \
  --scopes $VM_ID --condition "avg Percentage CPU > 80" --window-size 15m --evaluation-frequency 5m --severity 2 --action $AG
az monitor metrics alert create -n vm-memory-alert-normain-prod-01 -g $RG --subscription $SUB \
  --scopes $VM_ID --condition "avg Available Memory Bytes < 1073741824" --window-size 15m --evaluation-frequency 5m --severity 2 --action $AG
# Disk: per-data-disk metric "Data Disk Used Percentage" or guest-OS metrics if AMA installed
```

### Fix 2 — Add AOAI capacity alerts (≈ 45 min)
Per AI Services account, alert on:
- `ProcessedPromptTokens` rolling rate vs quota (>80% TPM)
- `AzureOpenAIRequests` 429 count > 0 (rate-limit hit)
- `Latency` p95 > threshold

```bash
for region in sweden germany eu-west norway france; do
  AOAI_ID=$(az resource show --subscription $SUB -g $RG -n ${region}-normain-prod-01 \
    --resource-type Microsoft.CognitiveServices/accounts --query id -o tsv)
  az monitor metrics alert create -n aoai-throttle-${region}-prod-01 -g $RG --subscription $SUB \
    --scopes $AOAI_ID --condition "total AzureOpenAIRequests where StatusCode includes 429 > 0" \
    --window-size 5m --evaluation-frequency 1m --severity 2 --action $AG
done
```

### Fix 3 — Capacity Management Plan doc + first review (≈ 30 min)
1-page markdown:
- **Scope:** prod VM, prod PSQL, prod Storage, prod AI Services (5 regions), Form Recognizer
- **Metrics + thresholds:** mirror the alerts above
- **Review cadence:** quarterly; owner = CTO
- **Forecast inputs:** AOAI TPM growth from past quota bumps; user-count growth from product
- **First review:** today's date, log of current utilization vs. capacity

Upload as Vanta evidence under CAP-7. Schedule recurring quarterly Calendar event.

